{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"I submitted the mitigation. The fix removes a stray label that was sending user traffic to the wrong pod.\n\n**Root cause:** The `search` deployment's pod template had a `service-route: frontend` label added in revision 2. The `frontend` Service selects on that label, so it was also routing to the search pod on port 5000, which doesn't serve that port.\n\n**Fix:** I removed the `service-route` label from the `search` pod template in `deploy/search`. The rollout completed, and `endpoints/frontend` now lists only `10.244.110.143:5000`, the frontend pod.\n\n**Not verified:** I did not measure request latency or error rates after the fix, so the submission's sustained-latency check is the first confirmation."}}
